-- title:
--   Flatness at p for Hecke points of level prime to p
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, a nonzero level $N$ and a finite set $S$ of natural numbers containing $p$ and containing every prime divisor of $N$. Let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a complete discrete valuation domain of characteristic zero with finite residue field in which $p$ lies in the maximal ideal, and let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) — the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$ — to $\mathcal{O}'$. Assume $p \nmid N$. Let $\rho$ be an adic Galois representation over $\mathcal{O}'$: a finite free $\mathcal{O}'$-module $V$ of rank $2$ with a monoid homomorphism $\sigma \mapsto \rho(\sigma)$ from $\operatorname{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal{O}'}(V)$ which is adically continuous, in the sense that for each $n$ there is a finite extension $L/\mathbb{Q}$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ such that every $\sigma$ fixing $L$ pointwise satisfies $\rho(\sigma)v - v \in \mathfrak{m}^n V$ for all $v$. Suppose that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $A \subset \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a nonunit of $A$, and every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, one has $\operatorname{charpoly}(\rho(\sigma)) = X^2 - \chi(T_\ell)X + \ell$. The conclusion is `ρ.IsFlatAt p`: the residue field of $\mathcal{O}'$ is finite, and for every ideal $I$ of $\mathcal{O}'$ with $\mathcal{O}'/I$ finite there exist a commutative ring $H$ carrying the structure of a cocommutative Hopf algebra over the subring of $\mathbb{Q}$ of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$, finite and flat over that subring, and a bijection $e$ from the set of algebra homomorphisms $H \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (with its convolution group law) onto $V/IV$ carrying products to sums and satisfying $e(g) = \rho(\sigma)\,e(f)$ on $V/IV$ whenever $g = \sigma \circ f$.
--
--   This is the finite-flatness (good reduction at $p$) input for the Galois representation attached to a $\mathcal{O}'$-valued weight-two Hecke eigensystem of level $N$ prime to $p$: classically it follows from good reduction of the modular Jacobian at $p$ together with the theory of finite flat group schemes over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$. Note that the hypothesis $p \nmid N$ is essential, and that the statement imposes the flatness condition on $\rho$ itself, characterised only through the Frobenius characteristic polynomials prescribed by $\chi$. It is used by [`CuspForm.exists_galoisRep_isFlatAt_of_point_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.exists_galoisRep_isFlatAt_of_point_of_not_dvd) and by [`CuspForm.isFlatAt_of_point_of_not_dvd_of_residual_isAbsolutelyIrreducible`](thm.html#CuspForm.isFlatAt_of_point_of_not_dvd_of_residual_isAbsolutelyIrreducible), which feed the flat deformation condition of the modularity-lifting argument.
